<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Guelph Bike Facilities &mdash; OSM Gaps</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../index.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="gaps.css">
<link rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
      integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY="
      crossorigin="">
<script defer src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
        integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo="
        crossorigin=""></script>
<script defer src="gaps.js"></script>
<script data-goatcounter="https://osm-guelph.goatcounter.com/count" async src="//gc.zgo.at/count.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="app">

<header class="bar">
  <div class="bar-head">
    <h1>Guelph Bike Facilities &mdash; what OSM is missing</h1>
    <a class="back" href="../">&larr; reference layer</a>
    <a class="back" href="history.html">gaps over time &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  <div class="counts">
    <div class="count headline new"><strong>{{NEW_COUNT}}</strong><span>new City installs ({{RECENT_SINCE}}+) not in OSM</span></div>
    <div class="count missing"><strong>{{MISSING_COUNT}}</strong><span>missing</span></div>
    <div class="count says_no"><strong>{{SAYS_NO_COUNT}}</strong><span>OSM says no</span></div>
    <div class="count nosep"><strong>{{NOSEP_COUNT}}</strong><span>no separation</span></div>
    <div class="count nobike"><strong>{{NOBIKE_COUNT}}</strong><span>footway, no bikes</span></div>
    <div class="count unsigned_route"><strong>{{UNSIGNED_COUNT}}</strong><span>unsigned route</span></div>
    <div class="count spot"><strong>{{SPOT_COUNT}}</strong><span>crossrides etc. (not counted)</span></div>
    <div class="count meta-count">City data {{DATA_DATE}} &middot; OSM data {{OSM_DATE}} &middot; compared {{BUILD_DATE}}</div>
  </div>
  {{OSM_NOTE}}
  <p class="note">
    OSM has {{LANE_POS_KM}} of the City's {{LANE_KM}}&nbsp;km of on-road lane
    on the right side of the road, and the buffer on {{SEP_OK_KM}} of the
    {{BUFFER_KM}}&nbsp;km where the City records one. Of what the City
    installed since {{RECENT_SINCE}}, {{RECENT_GAP_KM}} of
    {{RECENT_KM}}&nbsp;km is not in OSM yet. {{LANE_ANY_KM}}&nbsp;km of City
    lane is drawn on the road centreline, where its side cannot be read: those
    are judged on any side, and their rows say so.
  </p>
  <p class="licence">
    <a href="{{LICENSE_URL}}">{{LICENSE_NOTICE}}</a>
    Source: <a href="{{DATASET_PAGE}}">Bike Facilities</a>.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="layout">
  <div id="gap-map"
       data-geojson="gaps.geojson"
       data-raster="../tiles/raster/{z}/{x}/{y}.png"
       data-raster-minzoom="{{RASTER_MINZOOM}}"
       data-raster-maxzoom="{{RASTER_MAXZOOM}}"></div>

  <aside class="panel">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <div class="controls">
        <label title="Installed {{RECENT_SINCE}} or later, and not in OSM"><span class="swatch new"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-new" checked> New</label>
        <label title="Not in OSM: no lane tag on its side, no path, no separate cycleway"><span class="swatch missing"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-missing" checked> Missing</label>
        <label title="The OSM road says cycleway=no on the side the City has a lane"><span class="swatch says_no"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-says_no" checked> Says no</label>
        <label title="In OSM, but the City's curb, bollards or painted buffer is not tagged"><span class="swatch nosep"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-nosep" checked> No separation</label>
        <label title="A multi-use path mapped as a footway with no bicycle access"><span class="swatch nobike"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-nobike" checked> No bikes</label>
        <label title="A City signed route with no OSM route=bicycle relation and no cycleway tag"><span class="swatch unsigned_route"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-unsigned_route" checked> Unsigned route</label>
        <label title="City status Planned: not built yet ({{PLANNED_COUNT}} segments)"><span class="swatch planned"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-planned"> Planned</label>
        <label title="Crossrides, intersection treatments and curb cuts: no settled OSM tag, so shown and not counted ({{SPOT_COUNT}})"><span class="swatch spot"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-spot"> Crossrides etc.</label>
        <input type="search" id="filter" placeholder="Filter by street, type, tag or id...">
      </div>
      <p class="hint">
        Newest City installs first. Each row says what to add and where:
        <strong>iD</strong> opens the editor there (with the OSM way selected
        when there is one), <strong>JOSM</strong> loads the area into a
        running JOSM through remote control. Click a row to see it on the
        map, then press <kbd>I</kbd> for iD, <kbd>J</kbd> for JOSM or
        <kbd>O</kbd> for openstreetmap.org. <code>left</code> and
        <code>right</code> are relative to the direction of the OSM way.
        Coloured lines from z{{RASTER_MINZOOM}} are the City's own layer;
        check current imagery before adding anything.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table id="gap-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Year</th><th class="col-name">Street &middot; facility &middot; tag to add</th>
              <th>Status</th><th>Open</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>

</body>
</html>
